# AR Card Game with ZED Integration

## Project Overview
An augmented reality card game that combines mobile AR gameplay with a shared ZED display system, creating an immersive multiplayer experience in educational settings.

## Core Features
- **Multiplayer AR Card Game**: Support for 6 active players using mobile devices with Vuforia AR
- **ZED Integration**: Real-time visualization of the game map and gameplay elements on a large display
- **Spectator Mode**: Additional students can interact with game content through the ZED display
- **Cross-Platform Interaction**: Seamless connection between mobile AR and ZED display

## Technical Architecture

### Game Components
- **Mobile Client (Player)**
  - Unity Game Engine
  - Vuforia AR Framework
  - Netcode for GameObjects (Networking)
  - Custom UI/UX for card interactions

- **ZED Display System**
  - ZED SDK for 3D visualization
  - Unity integration for game state rendering
  - Real-time synchronization with game server

- **Server Infrastructure**
  - Netcode for GameObjects
  - Game state management
  - Player session handling
  - Real-time data synchronization

### Key Technologies
- Unity (Game Engine)
- Vuforia (AR Framework)
- ZED SDK (3D Display)
- Netcode for GameObjects (Networking)

## Target Environment
- **Players**: Mobile devices (iOS/Android) with AR capabilities
- **Display**: ZED camera system with projector setup
- **Network**: Local network for minimal latency

## Game Flow
1. Players join the game session using mobile devices
2. Each player uses AR markers to interact with their cards
3. Game state is synchronized across all devices
4. ZED display shows the complete game state including:
   - Game map
   - Active cards
   - Special effects
   - Player actions
5. Non-playing students can view and interact with displayed content

## Future Enhancements
- Advanced spectator interactions
- Enhanced AR visualization
- Additional game modes
- Educational analytics integration

## Setup Requirements
- Unity 2022.x or later
- Vuforia Engine
- ZED SDK
- Mobile devices with AR capabilities
- ZED camera
- Projection system

